    "text": {
     "en": "(additional, not in the textbook) A forest has many trees and is a home for many living things.\nTall trees give shade. Birds nest on branches and squirrels live in hollows.\nInsects live on the bark and leaves. Worms live in the soil.\nAll these living things share one place and depend on each other.\nWe should protect forests."
    }
